tattered black leather book dyes~
The book contains a number of natural items that can be used to create
colored dyes. Of interest is mainly the first page...

&rRed Dye&n    - Two portions of red berries, common in forested areas
Black Dye  - Two portions of bark from a logwood sapling
&YYellow Dye&n - Two portions of onion, common in farming communities
&cBlue Dye&n   - Two portions of leaves from the woad tree
&WWhite Dye&n  - One portion of white root, common in forested areas
&gGreen Dye&n  - One portion of white root, one onion and two woad leaves
&yOrange Dye&n - One portion of white root, two onions and red berries
&mPurple Dye&n - One portion of white root, red berries and two woad leaves
~
